    },
    {
      q: "Which Australian states observe Daylight Saving Time?",
      a: "Daylight Saving Time (DST) is observed in South Australia, New South Wales, Victoria, Tasmania, and the Australian Capital Territory. Queensland, Western Australia, and the Northern Territory do not observe DST, meaning their clocks remain on standard time year-round."
    },
    {
      q: "What are the standard dates for Daylight Saving Time in Australia?",
      a: "For the jurisdictions that observe DST, the period begins on the first Sunday of October (clocks go forward one hour at 2:00 a.m. standard time to 3:00 a.m. daylight time) and ends on the first Sunday of April (clocks go back one hour at 3:00 a.m. daylight time to 2:00 a.m. standard time)."
