  <section id="states-territories" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="Australian States &amp; Territories Guide">
    <h2>5. Australian States &amp; Territories Guide</h2>
    <p>
      Because time keeping is a state responsibility, it is important to analyze the exact time zone and DST rules for each Australian state, territory, and external dependency:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Western Australia (WA):</strong> Observes AWST (UTC+8) year-round. It does not observe DST. 
        A small border area near the South Australian border (including Eucla) observes Central Western Standard Time (CWST, UTC+8:45) year-round.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Northern Territory (NT):</strong> Observes ACST (UTC+9:30) year-round. It does not observe DST.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>South Australia (SA):</strong> Observes ACST (UTC+9:30) in winter and ACDT (UTC+10:30) in summer. It participates in standard seasonal DST changes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Queensland (QLD):</strong> Observes AEST (UTC+10) year-round. It does not observe DST.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>New South Wales (NSW):</strong> Observes AEST (UTC+10) in winter and AEDT (UTC+11) in summer. 
        The border community of Broken Hill observes Central Time (ACST/ACDT), and Lord Howe Island observes UTC+10:30 in winter with a 30-minute shift to UTC+11 in summer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Victoria (VIC):</strong> Observes AEST (UTC+10) in winter and AEDT (UTC+11) in summer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tasmania (TAS):</strong> Observes AEST (UTC+10) in winter and AEDT (UTC+11) in summer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Australian Capital Territory (ACT):</strong> Observes AEST (UTC+10) in winter and AEDT (UTC+11) in summer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>External Territories:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Norfolk Island:</strong> Observes UTC+11 Standard / UTC+12 Daylight (participates in DST).</li>
          <li><strong>Christmas Island:</strong> Observes UTC+7 year-round (no DST).</li>
          <li><strong>Cocos (Keeling) Islands:</strong> Observes UTC+6:30 year-round (no DST).</li>
          <li><strong>Macquarie Island:</strong> Observes UTC+11 year-round (no DST).</li>
          <li><strong>Heard and McDonald Islands:</strong> Observes UTC+5 year-round.</li>
          <li><strong>Antarctic Stations:</strong> Mawson Station uses UTC+5, Davis Station uses UTC+7, and Casey Station uses UTC+8.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

