    <h2>6. Australia Time Zone Map Explained</h2>
    <p>
      The Australian timezone map reveals how standard meridians correspond with regional population centers. 
      Instead of using simple vertical divisions, boundaries curve around local government areas to maintain community integration.
    </p>

    <p>
      For example, the boundary between Eastern and Central Time in New South Wales bends around Broken Hill. 
      Because Broken Hill is located near the South Australian border and is economically integrated with Adelaide, it legally observes Central Standard and Daylight Time rather than New South Wales Eastern Time.
    </p>

